A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate only when it has the **same known cause** as an existing report
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), superseding decision 0001):

1. Look up the tenant's locale and booking form, and check the report channel and body.
2. Compare causes using `causeOf` and `sameCause`; neither the subject nor the intake tag establishes a cause.
3. Merge only with the same known cause. Otherwise keep a separate ticket or investigate missing evidence.
4. Count each report ID once, because export pages can overlap.

<Callout>
Day-first booking-v3 form reports have a hint mismatch. Other affected day-first reports
have the shared-parser classification. A matching subject does not make these the same issue.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Do not merge unknown causes. Keep the report for review, get missing tenant metadata,
and preserve body evidence that conflicts with the assigned cause.

